// Renovate (GitHub App, https://github.com/apps/renovate): a pull request for each new release of
// what Jest Runner builds on, plus the "Dependency Dashboard" issue listing what is open. Their own
// pull requests: the test frameworks the end-to-end tests run for real (Jest, Vitest), the Babel
// parser that finds the tests in a file, Bun (packageManager in package.json, read by Renovate's npm
// manager) and the Node of CI (Jest runs on it). The VS Code API (engines.vscode,
// @types/vscode and the "VS Code 1.x or newer" of the docs) is never updated by Renovate.
// Everything else (the other packages, the actions, the images) comes with the shared settings of
// firsttris/workflows (renovate/default.json5): minor and patch updates once a month in one pull
// request that merges itself when CI is green, majors on request in the dashboard.
// Check with `bunx --package renovate renovate-config-validator .github/renovate.json5`.
{
  $schema: "https://docs.renovatebot.com/renovate-schema.json",
  extends: ["github>firsttris/workflows//renovate/default.json5"],
  customManagers: [
    {
      // engines.vscode, from the same releases as @types/vscode: vsce refuses a package whose
      // @types/vscode is newer than engines.vscode, so both take the same version
      customType: "regex",
      managerFilePatterns: ["/^package\\.json$/"],
      matchStrings: ['"engines": \\{\\s*"vscode": "\\^(?<currentValue>\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+)"'],
      depNameTemplate: "vscode-engine",
      packageNameTemplate: "@types/vscode",
      datasourceTemplate: "npm",
    },
    {
      // "VS Code 1.100 or newer" in the README and the docs
      customType: "regex",
      managerFilePatterns: ["/^README\\.md$/", "/^docs/(getting-started|development)\\.md$/"],
      matchStrings: ["VS Code (?<currentValue>\\d+\\.\\d+) or newer"],
      depNameTemplate: "vscode-docs",
      packageNameTemplate: "@types/vscode",
      datasourceTemplate: "npm",
      extractVersionTemplate: "^(?<version>\\d+\\.\\d+)\\.\\d+$",
      versioningTemplate: "regex:^(?<major>\\d+)\\.(?<minor>\\d+)$",
    },
    {
      // The Node of CI (the matrix of the test job, where Jest runs) and of docs/development.md
      customType: "regex",
      managerFilePatterns: ["/^\\.github/workflows/ci\\.yml$/", "/^docs/development\\.md$/"],
      matchStrings: [
        "node-version: \\[?(?<currentValue>\\d+)\\.x",
        "Node\\.js (?<currentValue>\\d+) \\(the version CI uses\\)",
        "with Bun and Node (?<currentValue>\\d+): `bun install",
      ],
      depNameTemplate: "node",
      datasourceTemplate: "node-version",
      versioningTemplate: "node",
    },
  ],
  packageRules: [
    {
      // The lowest VS Code the extension runs on. Raising it shuts out every editor still on an
      // older one (VSCodium, Cursor, Windsurf, Gitpod lag behind VS Code): with ^1.107.0 (January
      // 2026) and ^1.140.0 (#533, reverted) Jest Runner no longer showed up in Cursor's extension
      // search (#403). So Renovate never proposes it, not even in the Dependency Dashboard. Only
      // when a newer API is really needed: set `enabled: true` here, or raise engines.vscode,
      // @types/vscode and the docs by hand, after checking the forks' VS Code version.
      matchManagers: ["npm", "custom.regex"],
      matchPackageNames: ["@types/vscode"],
      enabled: false,
      rangeStrategy: "bump",
      groupName: "VS Code engine",
      commitMessageTopic: "VS Code engine",
      dependencyDashboardApproval: true,
      prBodyNotes: [
        "`engines.vscode`, `@types/vscode` and the \"VS Code 1.x or newer\" of README.md, docs/getting-started.md and docs/development.md move together (`vsce package` fails when `@types/vscode` is newer than `engines.vscode`). Before merging: is this API really needed? Check which VS Code version the forks on Open VSX are based on (VSCodium, Cursor, Windsurf); users on an older one get no more updates. The history went back down twice (\"lower engine version\"). Then `bun run typecheck`, `bun run build` and `bun run package`, and try the .vsix of this PR's CI in the oldest editor that should still work.",
      ],
      schedule: ["at any time"],
      automerge: false,
    },
    {
      // Jest: the e2e tests spawn real Jest processes; their results come from the JSON output
      matchManagers: ["npm"],
      matchPackageNames: ["jest", "babel-jest", "@types/jest"],
      enabled: true,
      groupName: "Jest",
      sourceUrl: "https://github.com/jestjs/jest",
      prBodyNotes: [
        "Jest runs the unit tests and is one of the frameworks the e2e tests (`bun run test:e2e`) start for real on Linux, Windows and macOS. A new major: read the changelog for the CLI options and the `--json` output (src/frameworkAdapters.ts, src/parsers); docs/frameworks.md names the supported versions. Users keep older Jest majors, so nothing may depend on the new one alone.",
      ],
      schedule: ["at any time"],
      automerge: false,
      dependencyDashboardApproval: false,
    },
    {
      // Vitest: the e2e tests spawn real Vitest processes with Jest Runner's reporter
      matchManagers: ["npm"],
      matchPackageNames: ["vitest"],
      enabled: true,
      groupName: "Vitest",
      sourceUrl: "https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest",
      prBodyNotes: [
        "The e2e tests run the new Vitest with Jest Runner's reporter (`vitest-reporter.cjs`) and the `-t` name filter. A new major: docs/frameworks.md says the reporter works with \"Vitest 2 to 5\" and the name filter matches \"the `suite test` format of Vitest 4 and the `suite > test` format of Vitest 5\"; check the reporter API and the test name format, keep the older majors working and update docs/frameworks.md and docs/internals/.",
      ],
      schedule: ["at any time"],
      automerge: false,
      dependencyDashboardApproval: false,
    },
    {
      // Babel parses the users' test files to find describe/it/test blocks
      matchManagers: ["npm"],
      matchPackageNames: ["@babel/**"],
      enabled: true,
      groupName: "Babel",
      sourceUrl: "https://github.com/babel/babel",
      prBodyNotes: [
        "`@babel/parser` and `@babel/traverse` find the tests in a file (src/parsers/jestParser/babelParser.ts, src/parsers/nodeTestParser.ts), so a change in the AST changes the CodeLens and the Test Explorer tree. The unit tests in src/test cover the parser; check the changelog for removed plugins or node types.",
      ],
      schedule: ["at any time"],
      automerge: false,
      dependencyDashboardApproval: false,
    },
    {
      // packageManager in package.json: setup-bun's bun-version-file in ci.yml
      matchPackageNames: ["bun"],
      groupName: "Bun",
      sourceUrl: "https://github.com/oven-sh/bun",
      prBodyNotes: [
        "`packageManager` in package.json is the Bun of every CI job. Bun installs the packages (`bun.lock`), runs the scripts and Vite (`bun --bun vite build`) and packages the `.vsix` (`vsce package --no-dependencies`); Jest itself runs on Node. Check that `ci.yml` stays green on Ubuntu, Windows and macOS, compare `unzip -l` of the `.vsix` artifact with the last release, and run `bun install` locally if `bun.lock` changes.",
      ],
      schedule: ["at any time"],
      automerge: false,
      dependencyDashboardApproval: false,
    },
    {
      matchPackageNames: ["node"],
      groupName: "Node",
      sourceUrl: "https://github.com/nodejs/node",
      prBodyNotes: [
        "The Node of CI, on which Jest and the e2e tests run (Bun installs and runs the scripts). The bundle's target (`node18` in vite.config.ts) follows the Node of the oldest supported VS Code, not this one.",
      ],
      schedule: ["at any time"],
      automerge: false,
      dependencyDashboardApproval: false,
    },
  ],
}
